"Ohai.ai | How It Works (https://www.ohai.ai/how-it-works/)\nciteturn93search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; \n\nFrequently Asked Questions\n\nWhy do I need an AI household assistant?\n\nModern families juggle calendars, emails, school portals, sports apps, and constant updates. Ohai reduces the mental load by turning all of that noise into one organized, unified plan, saving time, reducing stress, and preventing things from slipping through the cracks.\n\nDoes Ohai have a mobile app for iPhone and Android?\n\nYes. Ohai has a mobile app for both iPhone (iOS) and Android.\n\n  * iPhone users can download Ohai from the Apple App Store here.\n  * Android users can download Ohai from the Google Play Store here.\n\nWhat does O scan and sync?\n\nO can process and organize calendars, emails, PDFs, photos, school updates, sports schedules, newsletters, and other household information, turning all of it into structured events, tasks, and reminders.\n\nHow much does it cost?\n\nOhai offers flexible plans depending on how many people need access:\n• Individual Premium: $9.99 per month\n• Premium Plus (Duo): $19.99 per month\n• Premium Group: $29.99 per month\nA free trial is available for new users.\n\nIs my data private?\n\nYes. You choose exactly what to connect. Ohai only accesses sources you authorize and never sells or shares your data.\n\nHow does Ohai help me manage my household calendar?\n\nOhai syncs every connected calendar, scans events for important details, resolves conflicts, and keeps everything updated in one place. It sends reminders, handles schedule changes, and keeps your day organized automatically.\n\nHow does Ohai help with school and sports coordination?\n\nO scans emails, PDFs, district notices, sports apps, and newsletters to pull out schedules, closures, and updates, then adds everything to your family calendar without manual entry.\n\nHow does Ohai use AI for meal planning?\n\nOhai recommends meals based on your preferences, fits them into your schedule, creates a grocery list, and connects with Instacart so ingredients can be delivered when you need them.\n\nHow does Ohai keep tasks and to-dos organized?\n\nText, upload, or forward anything, Ohai turns notes, lists, and reminders into structured tasks with due dates, assignments, and smart follow-ups.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFamilyWall | About Us (https://www.prod.familywall.com/about.html)\nciteturn93search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; \n\n# About Us\n\n# About FamilyWall\n\n### Why FamilyWall?\n\nWe created FamilyWall because there was no digital service where you could simply and privately share information with your family.\n\nThink about it, most of your family connects to social networks to communicate with friends and professional colleagues, not with family. The reason - nobody wants to share their private life on social networks. Communication with your family remains limited to kitchen magnets, post-it notes left on a board, mobile texting or one-to-one email.\n\nHow often do you call your kids to know where they are? With FamilyWall, all your family can access a private cloud, exchange messages with all the members in your circle, share important contacts such as babysitters and doctors, organize family events, locate the last position posted by a member.\n\nAt FamilyWall, we believe in simplicity, privacy, great design, and we think we've been able to focus the app on what matters the most for you: Sharing with people you care about most.\n\nFamilyWall is PRIVATE, FREE, SECURE & AD-FREE.\n\n** At FamilyWall, your private life...stays private!. All your personal data will stay confidential and will never be used for commercial use. **\n\nDesigned to be present on all the connected devices of your home, FamilyWall is accessible on the web, on your iPhone, iPad, Android smartphones and tablets.\n\nFor more information on FamilyWall features, please click here to see more detai